WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.042
Multiple CTEs can depend on earlier CTEs.

00:00:04.042 --> 00:00:08.817
This creates a pipeline. The first stage summarizes admissions.

00:00:08.817 --> 00:00:12.672
The second stage joins those counts to patient attributes.

00:00:12.672 --> 00:00:16.087
The final query creates a visit-pattern label.

00:00:16.087 --> 00:00:20.902
Each stage has one focused job and one explainable grain.

00:00:20.902 --> 00:00:27.732
A CTE gives a name to an intermediate result so a complex query can be read in stages.

00:00:27.732 --> 00:00:35.572
Use it to clarify grain changes and major transformations, not simply to break every two lines into a

00:00:35.572 --> 00:00:42.320
new block. A useful CTE name describes what the rows represent, such as patient_totals or ranked_visits.
